<title>USA: Opponents campaign against Pa. sales tax hike.</title>
<headline>Opponents campaign against Pa. sales tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Opponents of a half-cent sales tax increase proposal for 10 Western Pennsylvania counties kicked off their anti-tax campaign.</p>
<p>The group, calling itself Good Sports Coalition, said the counties which vote for a sales tax increase will not see the benefits because only Allegheny and Pittsburgh will reap the rewards.</p>
<p>The November ballot will ask voters to approve the tax increase, with part of the money earmarked for a new professional baseball stadium in Pittsburgh and part for expanding the city's David Lawrence Convention Center.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
